# Legacy language prefixes → canonical root plus query-based English
/es      /   301
/en      /?lang=en   301
/es/     /   301
/en/     /?lang=en   301
/es/blog/*   /blog/:splat   301
/en/blog/*   /blog/:splat?lang=en   301
/contacto   /#contacto   301
/es/contacto   /#contacto   301
/en/contacto   /?lang=en#contacto   301

# NO global SPA fallback here: Cloudflare Pages already serves index.html for
# unmatched paths (default SPA behavior), and functions/[[path]].js handles the
# known app routes plus a branded 404. Adding a /* /index.html 200 rule here
# would run after the catch-all function and interfere with static assets.